rrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from  $y=4.$ This means that $y=4$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=1$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points downward too. In other words, both arrows point in the *same* direction on either side oft $y=1.$This means that $y=1$ is a node.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10267759-948c-5e21-b819-eea0a52b9c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360894} {:answer/id #uuid "21c0f117-930c-5f72-bd6c-e01d53d016cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360984} {:answer/id #uuid "8db2a840-a6b6-51d4-8f6c-92bd0dad5406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361466} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c1cb60-43c1-5cc0-a644-c5f45b9d687b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361644} {:answer/id #uuid "c000b11d-6918-5ea4-9dcf-dd56873b8480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c000b11d-6918-5ea4-9dcf-dd56873b8480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361695} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e224e7e-dfd1-5c42-9dff-859b4fa1ddef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #ed